      "problem": "Which of the following number lines gives the solution to $-3\\le 2x-1\\le 5?$",
      "worked_solution": "We isolate $x$  by applying the addition and multiplication principles, as usual.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3 & \\le 2x-1\\le 5 \\\\ -3+1 & \\le 2x-1+1\\le 5+1 \\\\ -2 & \\le 2x\\le 6 \\\\ \\frac{-2}{2} & \\le \\frac{2x}{2}\\le \\frac{6}{2} \\\\ -1 & \\le x\\le 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can represent this solution using a number line, as follows. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14225253/assets/76b6a19b3104f122989479a681709af3ca0bf8c05c59f76dc2c7707643980398.png)",
